WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:07.680
House of the Dragon Episode 4 is about secs,
secrets and lies – characters make dramatic

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.870
emotional choices that may have “unwanted
consequences”.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:17.560
The episode starts at Storm’s End, the castle
of House Baratheon.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:23.060
We hear thunder rumbling and wind gusting
in the background, because this place is famous

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.760
for its storms.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:30.910
The winds roar up from the Narrow Sea, and
slam into the walls of Storm’s End.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:36.519
According to legend, Storm’s End was built
by Durran Godsgrief – the gods kept destroying

00:00:36.519 --> 00:00:42.540
his castles so he rebuilt them stronger until
he finally built Storm’s End, a castle strong

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:47.750
enough and magic enough to withstand the fury
of the gods.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.850
The Lord of Storm’s End is Boremund Baratheon.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:56.300
We saw Boremund speak up for Rhaenys Targaryen
at the tournament in Episode 1, because Boremund

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.260
is Rhaenys’ uncle.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.100
Boremund is one of the great lords of Westeros,
ruling the stormlands – like the Starks

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:08.040
rule the north, and the Lannisters rule the
westerlands.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.340
Rhaenyra is here to find a husband.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:14.820
She’s on tour visiting castles to meet some
single men.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.320
Noble families often have tours like this
to find a marriage partner.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:25.050
The books describe one king meeting a thousand
single girls in one day – and it’s described

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:30.520
as a Cattle Show, cause the girls are all
lined up like farm animals.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:37.280
So, it’s not exactly romantic, and Rhaenyra
is not impressed by these men.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.620
This secsy single is from House Dondarrion
– the family of Beric Dondarrion in Game

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:43.770
of Thrones.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:50.920
Rhaenyra is not interested in his dry moat,
but the Dondarrion mentions Rhaenyra’s great-grandmother,

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:57.480
Queen Alysanne, the wife of King Jaehaerys,
who once visited the Dondarrion castle, Blackhaven.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:03.950
There, Alysanne was enthralled by a Dondarrion
who played sad songs on his harp.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:07.160
Blackhaven is also where Criston Cole is from.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.660
Criston’s dad worked for the Dondarrions
as a steward.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.450
And Criston fought with the Dondarrions against
Dornish incursions.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:19.260
The next candidate is a boy from House Blackwood,
in the riverlands.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.870
The Blackwoods are one of the only families
in the south who worship the Old Gods, like

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.420
the Starks do.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:29.450
The Blackwood gets insulted by this guy from
House Bracken.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:34.150
Because the Blackwoods and the Brackens have
an ancient blood feud – these families have

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:37.930
hated and fought each other for thousands
of years.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:42.550
The Blackwoods say that the Brackens poisoned
their sacred weirwood tree.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:47.450
King Jaehaerys tried to make peace between
these families but it didn’t last.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:52.480
At one point, the Blackwoods and Brackens
fight for control of a pair of hills called

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:58.459
the Teats, and they argue over whose boobs
the hills are named after – are they Barba

00:02:58.459 --> 00:03:02.040
Bracken’s Teats or Missy Blackwood’s Teats.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:06.370
In the main series, the Brackens side with
the Lannisters, while the Blackwoods support

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.650
the Starks.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:12.630
And Lord Tytos Blackwood has a cool cloak.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:17.010
So the Blackwoods are fan favourites among
book readers.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:22.980
But when the Bracken insults the Blackwood
kid, Rhaenyra says she likes the Bracken – seems

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:28.730
like Rhaenyra is attracted to bad boys and
bullies – like her uncle Daemon.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:32.670
Rhaenyra still wears the necklace that Daemon
gave her.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:38.430
The Blackwood kid has enough of the Bracken’s
insults, so they fight, and the Blackwood

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.319
kills the Bracken.

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:45.569
This is another example of random violence
breaking out when it’s not meant to – like

00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:49.400
those knights killing each other in Episode
1.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:54.980
Like Rhaenys said, there are a lot of young
dumb men in the realm who are eager to fight

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:59.160
for glory after these long decades of peace.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:04.670
Some of these other eligible bachelors are
from houses Tully, Swann, Frey, and House

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:05.910
Mudd.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:12.970
And the Mudd is weird, because House Mudd
went extinct.. about four thousand years ago.

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:18.840
The castle of the Mudd kings has been a ruin
for so long that no one remembers its name.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:23.870
So this guy telling Rhaenyra he’s a Mudd
is kinda like telling your first date that

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:26.229
you’re an Egyptian pharaoh.

00:04:26.229 --> 00:04:32.419
That said, in the books there are some characters
who claim to be descendants of House Mudd.

00:04:32.419 --> 00:04:37.660
Including the mysterious Jenny of Oldstones,
who Podrick sings a song about in Game of

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:38.909
Thrones.

00:04:38.909 --> 00:04:43.319
Rhaenyra gets sick of the speed dating, and
heads back to King’s Landing, even though

00:04:43.319 --> 00:04:46.729
she was meant to keep touring for two more
months.

00:04:46.729 --> 00:04:52.469
Daemon Targaryen also returns, after he was
off at war on the Stepstones.

00:04:52.469 --> 00:04:58.779
Daemon swoops his dragon dangerously over
Rhaenyra’s ship, because Daemon is desperate

00:04:58.779 --> 00:05:02.979
for attention, and never misses the chance
to cause some chaos.

00:05:02.979 --> 00:05:10.319
In this episode, Daemon’s disruptive behaviour
rocks the boat both literally and metaphorically.

00:05:10.319 --> 00:05:15.580
When Daemon returns, the mood at court is
tense, cause last time Daemon was here, his

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:20.810
brother King Viserys exiled him and removed
him as heir to the Throne.

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:25.770
Then Daemon practically rebelled against Viserys,
and stole a dragon egg.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:31.059
So now Viserys tries to show strength and
authority by meeting Daemon in the throne

00:05:31.059 --> 00:05:36.279
room, wearing his crown, and holding the royal
sword Blackfyre.

00:05:36.279 --> 00:05:42.589
Daemon presents the hammer of the Crabfeeder,
who Daemon killed last episode.

00:05:42.589 --> 00:05:47.499
This is the hammer that the Crabfeeder used
to nail people to the beach to die.

00:05:47.499 --> 00:05:53.300
Daemon says he copied the Crabfeeder’s brutal
execution method, using to kill thousands

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:54.930
of Triarchy men.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:06:00.659
So like when he killed and mutilated people
with his gold cloaks, Daemon again uses violence

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:02.900
to create fear.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:09.930
Daemon says to add the hammer to the Iron
Throne, to join the other weapons of the Targaryens’

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:14.690
defeated enemies – Barristan says the same
thing in Game of Thrones.

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:20.780
Daemon wears a crown, and calls himself “King
of the Narrow Sea”, which is the ocean north

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.380
of the Stepstones.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:27.899
It is provocative to call himself king, as
though he’s the equal of Viserys.

00:06:27.899 --> 00:06:31.080
But then Daemon kneels and gives up his crown.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:37.400
So Daemon makes his homecoming dramatic and
theatrical, seeking glory and validation for

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.029
his accomplishments.

00:06:39.029 --> 00:06:44.430
In the books, Daemon’s return is even more
dramatic – Daemon swoops down on his dragon

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:47.900
during a tournament to give Viserys his crown.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:51.949
Viserys forgives Daemon’s crimes, and the
brothers reunite.

00:06:51.949 --> 00:06:57.840
They have a boozy garden party and talk about
their childhood – the books say that Viserys

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:04.539
loves Daemon because he remembers the fun
adventurous boy Daemon was, and tries to ignore

00:07:04.539 --> 00:07:07.939
the violent selfish man he’s become.

00:07:07.939 --> 00:07:13.110
Viserys mentions their mother Alyssa, and
how she was rebel who broke rules.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:16.669
Alyssa was a tomboy, kinda like Arya Stark.

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:22.110
She had a crooked broken nose from playing
with a wooden sword, and her eyes were two

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:23.499
different colours.

00:07:23.499 --> 00:07:28.490
Alyssa’s two favourite activities were having
secs with her husband Baelon, and riding her

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:30.599
dragon Meleys.

00:07:30.599 --> 00:07:36.439
Alyssa took her sons Viserys and Daemon on
dragon rides when they were just babies.

00:07:36.439 --> 00:07:40.249
Then Alyssa died young from childbirth complications.

00:07:40.249 --> 00:07:44.699
And now Rhaenys Targaryen rides Alyssa’s
dragon Meleys.

00:07:44.699 --> 00:07:47.529
Rhaenyra and Alicent start to reconnect.

00:07:47.529 --> 00:07:49.610
Cause Alicent feels lonely.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:53.830
Everyone treats her as a queen, not as a friend.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:59.559
She feels trapped in this castle, making babies
all day – Alicent has now given birth to

00:07:59.559 --> 00:08:03.249
a daughter, her second child after Aegon.

00:08:03.249 --> 00:08:08.429
Alicent envies Rhaenyra’s freedom in getting
to choose a husband – Alicent didn’t get

00:08:08.429 --> 00:08:13.139
to choose her husband – her father Otto
pushed to be with Viserys.

00:08:13.139 --> 00:08:18.749
Rhaenyra had been angry at Alicent for suddenly
marrying her dad, and becoming a political

00:08:18.749 --> 00:08:19.749
rival.

00:08:19.749 --> 00:08:24.149
But now she’s sympathetic, and they hold
hands again, like they used to.

00:08:24.149 --> 00:08:29.709
This moment of friendship makes it more painful
later when their relationship is threatened

00:08:29.709 --> 00:08:30.709
again.

00:08:30.709 --> 00:08:36.770
Rhaenyra speaks with Daemon in the Valyrian
language, which is their way of speaking secretly

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:38.450
and intimately.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:42.401
Rhaenyra tells Daemon that she doesn’t want
to get married because she doesn’t want

00:08:42.401 --> 00:08:47.880
to be trapped and lonely like Alicent, and
she doesn’t want to die in childbirth like

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:54.140
her mother Aemma did – and like her grandmother
Alyssa died of childbirth, and her other grandmother

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.820
Daella also died in childbirth.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:09:03.350
But Daemon says you shouldn’t live alone,
or in fear, or else you’ll miss out on life.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:07.530
You’ve got to take risks, break rules, do
what you want.

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:14.490
Daemon’s life philosophy sounds inspiring,
but Daemon also has a hidden motivation – Daemon

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:18.130
hopes to have secs with Rhaenyra, and to marry
her.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:24.930
So he plays the creepy uncle, giving Rhaenyra
wine, telling her she’s matured.

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:28.710
Rhaenyra asks why Daemon returned, what does
he want?

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:32.690
And it seems like what he wants is Rhaenyra.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:35.450
We see a meeting of the small council.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:39.430
Tyland Lannister is now master of ships to
replace Corlys.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:44.680
And now Rhaenyra is on the council, she has
a small council ball and everything.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:50.070
Looks like Viserys is finally including Rhaenyra,
so she can learn politics, which is /super

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:52.570
important for the heir to the Throne.

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:56.370
The council is worried about Corlys Velaryon.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:10:01.520
Despite Daemon calling himself King of the
Narrow Sea, it sounds like Corlys now controls

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:02.660
the region.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:08.810
And now, Corlys plans to marry his daughter
Laena to the son of the Sealord of Braavos.

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:14.480
Braavos is a city in the east – it’s where
Arya Stark joined the Faceless Men in Game

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:15.580
of Thrones.

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:19.030
&lt;Westeros usually gets along okay with Braavos.

00:10:19.030 --> 00:10:24.350
But Braavos is powerful – they’re very
rich, and have a strong navy.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:28.474
So Otto is worried that if Braavos allies
with the Velaryons with their wealth and ships,

00:10:28.474 --> 00:10:35.350
their combined strength could dominate the
Narrow Sea, and become a threat to the Targaryens.

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:40.660
Corlys is still angry that Viserys rejected
Laena’s marriage proposal.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:46.220
Otto says he learned about Corlys’ plans
from his brother Hobert in Oldtown.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:47.300
Which is weird.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:53.020
Why would Hobert in Oldtown know about Corlys
Velaryon’s plans?

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:57.080
Well Oldtown is the home of the Citadel of
the maesters.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:11:00.970
And the maesters send the letters between
the lords of Westeros.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:06.480
So maybe the Hightowers are using the maesters
to spy on lords across the realm.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:11.370
There are hints in the books of a maester
conspiracy.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:14.810
That night, Daemon leaves a message for Rhaenyra.

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:19.180
It shows her a secret passage out of her room
in the Red Keep.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:23.020
The Red Keep was built by King Maegor the
Cruel.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:27.860
And Maegor filled the Keep with secret passages,
hidden doors and steps.

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:31.960
There are a tunnels to escape the castle in
case of attack.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:37.980
There are spaces in the walls so that child
spies can listen to conversations.

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:42.950
After the Red Keep was built, Maegor had all
the construction workers killed, so that his

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:46.220
secret passages would stay secret.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:52.010
In Game of Thrones, Varys knows these passages,
and uses them free Tyrion.

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.950
In Hot D, Daemon knows the passages.

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:59.890
Previously, we saw him spying on the small
council from some hidden place.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:05.960
Now he uses a passage to sneak Rhaenyra out
of the castle, for a night on the town of

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:08.110
freedom and fun.

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:13.150
Disguised in different clothes, and with a
hat, Rhaenyra is freed from the restrictions

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:14.740
of being a princess.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:17.520
She’s thrilled to be mistaken for a boy.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:23.490
It’s like when Arya pretends to be a boy,
and experiences life as a common person.

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:27.990
We see a street performer doing what looks
like fire magic.

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:30.740
Or it might just be a cheap trick.

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:36.760
In the books, Melisandre mentions using flammable
powders instead of real magic.

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:42.780
But in Book 2, Daenerys sees a fire magic
performance, and Quaithe says the magic is

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:43.780
real.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:49.700
She says that magic is now more powerful because
Daenerys hatched dragons.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:54.240
It seems that when there are dragons in the
world, magic is stronger.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:13:00.760
In the time of Hot D, there are lots of dragons,
so this might be an especially magical time

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.330
in Westeros.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:06.000
Maybe that’s why Viserys has prophetic dreams.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:11.860
Rhaenyra and Daemon see a street theatre show,
like the one Arya sees in Braavos.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:15.810
This reveals how the common people feel about
the royal family.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:19.640
We see Daemon in his armour, and Rhaenyra
in her dress.

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:22.450
And baby Aegon with his dragon toy.

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:27.860
We learn that many common people want baby
Aegon to inherit the Throne, not Rhaenyra

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:33.040
– because Aegon is male, while Rhaenyra
is a “feeble” female.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:39.140
Rhaenyra says the common people don’t matter,
their desires are of “no consequence”.

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:45.050
Rhaenyra used those same words, “no consequence”,
when she told Viserys that her own desires

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.310
don’t matter.

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:51.680
Rhaenyra feels like no one cares about her
opinion, so why should she care about any

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:53.080
else’s?

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:58.200
But we saw in Game of Thrones that the common
people do matter – when they turn against

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:04.200
the Lannisters, they start a deadly riot,
and support the sparrows overthrowing Cersei.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:10.330
Good politicians know that to be a successful
ruler, you’ve got to win over the people.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:15.300
Rhaenyra steals food from a street vendor,
just for the thrill of breaking rules.

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:21.440
And she bumps into Harwin Strong – the son
of Lyonel Strong, who we met last episode.

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:25.190
Harwin has joined the gold cloaks City Watch
while his family’s at court.

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:28.180
And Daemon was once the commander of the gold
cloaks.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:33.060
So Harwin lets Rhaenyra continue on her secret
night-time adventure.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:39.370
Daemon takes Rhaenyra to a secs club, to show
her that secs is not just an obligation in

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:41.960
marriage to produce babies.

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:44.500
Secs can be for pleasure and passion.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:50.310
These opulent orgies fit with the theme of
decadence – this is a time of prosperity,

00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:56.529
indulgence and carefree pleasure – like
Rome before the fall.

00:14:56.529 --> 00:15:02.540
While Rhaenyra enjoys fun and freedom, Queen
Alicent is stuck at home, looking cold and

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:03.820
lonely.

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:09.790
Alicent gives a sponge bath to her husband
Viserys, whose body is falling apart from

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:12.840
the infection that started in his hand.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:18.130
In the books, Alicent cared for the old king
Jaehaerys like this while he was sick, helping

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:20.350
to bathe and dress him.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:25.010
The jester Mushroom claims that Alicent also
had secs with Jaehaerys.

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:31.430
There are also rumours that Alicent had secs
with Viserys before his wife Aemma died.

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:35.760
And Mushroom claims that Alicent lost her
virginity to Daemon.

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:41.930
So believe it or not, the books have even
more secret scandalous secs rumours than this

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:43.310
episode does.

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:48.450
Later, Viserys and Alicent have secs, and
Alicent gets no pleasure.

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:54.600
For her, secs is a duty where her body is
used to produce children.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:16:00.230
We see Alicent fidgeting with her fingers
– a sign of anxiety and discomfort.

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:05.830
Afterwards, she sees a mouse or rat on the
bed – which might represent corruption and

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:10.690
sickness, or that Viserys has been eating
cheese in bed.

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:16.500
So while Alicent is trapped in a bad secsual
experience, Rhaenyra explores the pleasure

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.230
of her secsuality.

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:21.550
She and her uncle Daemon start hooking up.

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:23.100
And Rhaenyra’s into it.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:27.400
But then Daemon stops, and just.. walks away.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:32.060
According to the show’s creators, Daemon
wanted to shock Rhaenyra, he wanted to be

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:38.060
in control of this situation, but he was thrown
off when Rhaenyra was more passionate and

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:40.190
into this than he was.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:44.960
Deep down Daemon knew that using Rhaenyra
was wrong.

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:50.620
So suddenly he felt impotent, unable to continue
– like previously when he stopped having

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:52.180
secs with Mysaria.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:54.420
So Daemon leaves.

00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:56.800
Rhaenyra is unsatisfied.

00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:02.680
So when she gets back to the Keep, she playfully
flirts with Ser Criston, kisses him, and takes

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:05.510
off his Kingsguard armour.

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:12.240
Criston is reluctant because as a Kingsguard
knight, he has sworn to never have secs, and

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:16.509
he especially can’t have secs with the princess
– that’s treason.

00:17:16.509 --> 00:17:21.740
In the books, a Kingsguard knight called Terrence
Toyne gets executed for the crime of having

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.980
secs with a king’s mistress.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:29.720
A knight called Lucamore Strong, a relative
of Lyonel and Harwin Strong, was found to

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:36.360
have secretly had three wives and fathered
sixteen children while on the Kingsguard.

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:41.490
So King Jaehaerys had Lucamore’s penis cut
off and sent him to the Night’s Watch.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:44.059
So Criston knows the danger here.

00:17:44.059 --> 00:17:46.460
But.. he wants Rhaenyra.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:50.519
And he may feel obligated to obey his princess.

00:17:50.519 --> 00:17:57.059
So Criston feels deeply conflicted as he puts
down his white Kingsguard cloak.

00:17:57.059 --> 00:18:02.039
In the books, a Kingsguard knight called Arys
has secs with Arianne Martell.

00:18:02.039 --> 00:18:06.070
Arys doesn’t want to soil his white cloak
by having secs.

00:18:06.070 --> 00:18:10.279
But Arianne says there’s no harm in love
– knights should be judged for how they

00:18:10.279 --> 00:18:14.130
use their sword, not for how they use their
cock.

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:19.909
So Rhaenyra and Criston have secs, and it
feels playful and joyous as the princess loses

00:18:19.909 --> 00:18:22.990
her virginity to the white knight.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:27.869
The next morning, Rhaenyra is happy to see
Criston – maybe she wants to continue this

00:18:27.869 --> 00:18:29.919
dangerous relationship.

00:18:29.919 --> 00:18:35.789
Rhaenyra no longer wears Daemon’s necklace
– Criston is the one she wants now.

00:18:35.789 --> 00:18:40.820
But Criston looks worried and distant, terrified
that he’ll be found out and punished.

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:46.960
A Song of Ice and Fire is full of these forbidden
romances – like Jon Snow and Ygritte – and

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:50.889
many of these relationships end in tragedy.

00:18:50.889 --> 00:18:56.760
In the books, the jester Mushroom has a very
different version of what happened between

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:59.110
Rhaenyra, Criston and Daemon.

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:02.970
Mushroom claims that Rhaenyra originally wanted
Criston.

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:08.929
So Daemon gave Rhaenyra secs lessons to teach
Rhaenyra how to seduce Criston.

00:19:08.929 --> 00:19:14.669
But, according to Mushroom, Criston rejected
Rhaenyra and kept to his Kingsguard vows.

00:19:14.669 --> 00:19:20.370
A big theme of the book Fire &amp; Blood is that
the historians are often wrong and don’t

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:24.820
know the real story of what happened behind
closed doors.

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:31.259
Daemon wakes up extremely hung over – looks
like he tried to drink enough to forget that

00:19:31.259 --> 00:19:32.970
he macked on his niece.

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:37.100
Daemon’s ex-lover Mysaria gave him a place
to crash.

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:40.950
It sounds like Daemon and Mysaria haven’t
seen each other in years.

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:47.910
Mysaria reveals she’s no longer a secs worker
– she’s now a spymaster, known as the

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:49.030
White Worm.

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:54.100
Cause when Rhaenyra leaves the secs club,
she’s seen by a young boy.

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:59.879
And that boy then goes to Otto Hightower and
tells him that Rhaenyra had secs with Daemon.

00:19:59.879 --> 00:20:05.399
Now the boy brings money back to Mysaria – payment
for the information.

00:20:05.399 --> 00:20:09.860
So instead of selling secs, Mysaria now sells
secrets.

00:20:09.860 --> 00:20:16.100
It’s like how Littlefinger in Game of Thrones
uses brothels both for selling secs, and for

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:17.500
spying.

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:21.919
But why would Mysaria tell Otto about Daemon
and Rhaenyra?

00:20:21.919 --> 00:20:24.450
That’ll get Daemon in trouble.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:30.059
Maybe Mysaria wants to hurt Daemon, as revenge
for abandoning her, and for using her in his

00:20:30.059 --> 00:20:31.450
Dragonstone plots.

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:36.669
Otto says that Mysaria is a trusted source
of information, like they’ve been working

00:20:36.669 --> 00:20:38.360
together for a while.

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:44.149
So maybe it was Mysaria who told Otto about
Daemon’s heir for a day speech in Episode

00:20:44.149 --> 00:20:45.149
1.

00:20:45.149 --> 00:20:49.330
Maybe she’s been working against Daemon
all along.

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:54.429
Then again, Daemon did want to be seen with
Rhaenyra at the secs club – he took off

00:20:54.429 --> 00:20:57.669
Rhaenyra’s hat, so she’d be recognised.

00:20:57.669 --> 00:21:02.369
So maybe Daemon wanted Mysaria to tell Otto
that he hooked up with Rhaenyra.

00:21:02.369 --> 00:21:08.059
Cause if people think Rhaenyra’s been devirginized
by Daemon, it’s more likely he’ll be allowed

00:21:08.059 --> 00:21:09.950
to marry Rhaenyra.

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:14.169
But does Mysaria know that Daemon wants Otto
to know?

00:21:14.169 --> 00:21:18.210
The whole Mysaria situation is mysterious.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:21.750
So Otto finds out that Daemon hooked up with
Rhaenyra.

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:25.380
And this is a big opportunity for him politically.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:30.860
Because if he can discredit Rhaenyra and Daemon,
that makes it more likely that his grandson

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:34.049
Aegon will become heir to the Throne instead.

00:21:34.049 --> 00:21:40.049
But Otto also knows that this news will hurt
Viserys, and the showrunners say that despite

00:21:40.049 --> 00:21:45.259
all his plotting, Otto does love Viserys and
doesn’t want to hurt him.

00:21:45.259 --> 00:21:50.059
Nonetheless, Otto tells Viserys that his daughter
had secs with his brother.

00:21:50.059 --> 00:21:51.629
And Viserys get angry.

00:21:51.629 --> 00:21:57.770
He accuses Otto of trying to undermine Rhaenyra
to get Aegon on the Throne – which is true.

00:21:57.770 --> 00:22:03.320
Viserys finally starts to realise that his
trusted Hand is corrupt – just like his

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:07.220
actual hand is infected.

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:09.639
Alicent overhears this conversation.

00:22:09.639 --> 00:22:14.369
So then Alicent confronts Rhaenyra about her
having secs with Daemon.

00:22:14.369 --> 00:22:19.519
Alicent is angry because a princess having
secs out of wedlock is seen as a terrible

00:22:19.519 --> 00:22:24.990
scandalous dishonour, not only to Rhaenyra
but to the whole royal family.

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:30.249
Rhaenyra losing her virginity makes her a
less desirable wife, which could make it harder

00:22:30.249 --> 00:22:32.929
to make a good marriage alliance.

00:22:32.929 --> 00:22:38.890
Incest and adultery are considered sins by
the Faith of the Seven, and Alicent is a devout

00:22:38.890 --> 00:22:40.019
believer.

00:22:40.019 --> 00:22:44.509
Some people like Daemon don’t care about
these rules – he thinks Targaryens can do

00:22:44.509 --> 00:22:45.619
what they want.

00:22:45.619 --> 00:22:48.280
But Alicent is a proper lady, she lives by
these rules.

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:51.179
She’s trapped in these rules.

00:22:51.179 --> 00:22:53.419
So maybe Alicent feels envious of Rhaenyra.

00:22:53.419 --> 00:22:57.519
It seems unfair that Rhaenyra gets to do what
she wants, while Alicent is trapped in a lonely

00:22:57.519 --> 00:22:59.690
marriage with Viserys.

00:22:59.690 --> 00:23:06.570
Alicent may also feel scared that if Rhaenyra
is punished and sent away, Alicent could lose

00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:08.580
her only friend.

00:23:08.580 --> 00:23:13.309
When Rhaenyra is faced with this dangerous
allegation, she lies.

00:23:13.309 --> 00:23:17.850
She swears on her mother’s memory that Daemon
didn’t touch her.

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:20.000
Which he totally did.

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:25.770
Making a false oath like this is pretty bad
in Westeros – especially in front of a weirwood

00:23:25.770 --> 00:23:26.770
tree.

00:23:26.770 --> 00:23:31.190
Rhaenyra and Alicent don’t believe in the
Old Gods religion, but symbolically there’s

00:23:31.190 --> 00:23:35.320
a sense that the Old Gods see Rhaenyra’s
lie.

00:23:35.320 --> 00:23:39.779
How will Alicent react if she finds out this
lie?

00:23:39.779 --> 00:23:44.499
Alicent and Rhaenyra’s relationship is probably
the longest and most intimate relationship

00:23:44.499 --> 00:23:46.269
in both of their lives.

00:23:46.269 --> 00:23:49.390
They grew up together, they love each other.

00:23:49.390 --> 00:23:54.119
So secrets between them can leave deep painful
wounds.

00:23:54.119 --> 00:23:59.059
Later, Alicent tells Viserys that she believes
Rhaenyra is innocent.

00:23:59.059 --> 00:24:00.820
She sticks up for her friend.

00:24:00.820 --> 00:24:04.370
Which makes it all the more tragic that Rhaenyra
lied.

00:24:04.370 --> 00:24:09.629
Viserys confronts Daemon, angry at him for
having secs with Rhaenyra.

00:24:09.629 --> 00:24:14.429
Of course, Daemon didn’t have secs with
Rhaenyra, but Daemon lets Viserys believe

00:24:14.429 --> 00:24:15.429
that he did.

00:24:15.429 --> 00:24:21.159
Cause if Rhaenyra is no longer a virgin, it’ll
be harder to marry her off – so Daemon says

00:24:21.159 --> 00:24:23.679
he’ll marry Rhaenyra.

00:24:23.679 --> 00:24:26.530
And this is a political move by Daemon.

00:24:26.530 --> 00:24:29.009
Cause Rhaenyra is heir to the Throne.

00:24:29.009 --> 00:24:32.899
As her husband, Daemon could potentially rule
Westeros.

00:24:32.899 --> 00:24:39.330
So it looks like this was Daemon’s plan
all along – to use Rhaenyra to get the Throne,

00:24:39.330 --> 00:24:41.149
and to piss off Viserys.

00:24:41.149 --> 00:24:46.990
Daemon resents Viserys for exiling him, for
not making him Hand, for not giving him the

00:24:46.990 --> 00:24:49.629
love and validation he wants.

00:24:49.629 --> 00:24:55.450
Daemon succeeds in pissing off Viserys, but
he fails to get Rhaenyra as wife.

00:24:55.450 --> 00:25:01.870
Viserys says no partly because Daemon is already
married to his estranged wife Rhea.

00:25:01.870 --> 00:25:07.710
And while the Faith has accepted Targaryen
incest, the Faith is not okay with Targaryen

00:25:07.710 --> 00:25:08.710
polygamy.

00:25:08.710 --> 00:25:13.330
Viserys exiles Daemon again, tells him to
go back to his estranged wife in the Vale

00:25:13.330 --> 00:25:15.730
and to never come back.

00:25:15.730 --> 00:25:17.570
Then Viserys confronts Rhaenyra.

00:25:17.570 --> 00:25:23.659
And he tells her that her.. personal desires
aren’t as important as the strength of the

00:25:23.659 --> 00:25:25.029
Targaryen dynasty.

00:25:25.029 --> 00:25:29.799
Because of Aegon the Conqueror’s dream,
his prophecy that the Targaryens will save

00:25:29.799 --> 00:25:32.200
the world from the white walkers.

00:25:32.200 --> 00:25:37.830
Aegon wrote a message on his Valyrian steel
dagger, that only appears when it’s in fire,

00:25:37.830 --> 00:25:39.600
&gt;like the One Ring.

00:25:39.600 --> 00:25:42.039
And it says “From my blood...

00:25:42.039 --> 00:25:47.799
come the prince that was promised... and his
will be the song of ice and fire”.

00:25:47.799 --> 00:25:49.840
So – what does that mean?

00:25:49.840 --> 00:25:55.330
The prince that was promised, or Azor Ahai,
is a prophesied hero, the chosen one who will

00:25:55.330 --> 00:25:58.379
lead the war against the white walkers.

00:25:58.379 --> 00:26:03.100
In the Game of Thrones show, Melisandre thinks
Stannis is the prince that was promised, then

00:26:03.100 --> 00:26:09.529
she thinks it’s Jon, then she thinks both
Jon and Daenerys “have a role to play”.

00:26:09.529 --> 00:26:15.429
So then Jon and Daenerys help in the battle
when Arya kills the Night King – using Aegon’s

00:26:15.429 --> 00:26:16.600
Valyrian steel dagger.

00:26:16.600 --> 00:26:20.279
In the books, the prophecy stuff is more complicated.

00:26:20.279 --> 00:26:25.039
It’s said that the hero will use a burning
sword called Lightbringer that might be a

00:26:25.039 --> 00:26:26.039
literal sword, or a metaphor for dragons or
something.

00:26:26.039 --> 00:26:29.970
There are themes of sacrifice that might connect
to Jon killing Daenerys.

00:26:29.970 --> 00:26:35.970
“the song of ice and fire” is a line from
Book 2, when Daenerys has a vision of her

00:26:35.970 --> 00:26:36.999
brother Rhaegar.

00:26:36.999 --> 00:26:43.570
Rhaegar says his son is the prince that was
promised, and “his is the song of ice and

00:26:43.570 --> 00:26:44.570
fire”.

00:26:44.570 --> 00:26:48.870
Rhaegar does change his mind a lot about who
the prince that was promised is, but there

00:26:48.870 --> 00:26:53.940
are lots of hints that Rhaegar’s son Jon
Snow is probably the chosen one.

00:26:53.940 --> 00:27:01.090
Jon is the son of an icy Stark and a fiery
Targaryen making him a song or a son of ice

00:27:01.090 --> 00:27:02.279
and fire.

00:27:02.279 --> 00:27:09.019
Ned Stark promises to protect Jon, which makes
Jon literally a prince that was promised.

00:27:09.019 --> 00:27:14.539
So it looks like in the books, Jon will play
a bigger role in defeating the white walkers

00:27:14.539 --> 00:27:18.779
– he won’t just shout at a dragon while
Arya saves the day like in the show.

00:27:18.779 --> 00:27:23.529
But prophecies are ambiguous, and the book
series still isn’t finished, so it’s still

00:27:23.529 --> 00:27:26.210
a mystery how the books will end.

00:27:26.210 --> 00:27:30.639
The point of all this is that the Targaryen
Throne is a huge responsibility.

00:27:30.639 --> 00:27:35.850
It’s not just about personal desires, it’s
about protecting the bloodline that will save

00:27:35.850 --> 00:27:37.009
the world.

00:27:37.009 --> 00:27:42.769
So Rhaenyra should not undermine their strength
and stability by rooting her uncle.

00:27:42.769 --> 00:27:48.320
Viserys says the old king Jaehaerys would
have disinherited Rhaenyra for this.

00:27:48.320 --> 00:27:53.429
Because Jaehaerys had similar trouble with
his daughter Saera, when Saera had secret

00:27:53.429 --> 00:27:54.909
scandalous secs.

00:27:54.909 --> 00:28:01.809
Jaehaerys was furious, said Saera was no longer
his daughter, and Saera ran off to a brothel

00:28:01.809 --> 00:28:03.129
in the east.

00:28:03.129 --> 00:28:08.899
Of course it is very unfair that women aren’t
allowed secsual freedom, while men can generally

00:28:08.899 --> 00:28:11.369
root who they want without consequence.

00:28:11.369 --> 00:28:15.989
Viserys says the time for childish rebellion
is over.

00:28:15.989 --> 00:28:22.649
He says Rhaenyra she will marry Laenor Velaryon,
the son and heir of Lord Corlys, and the rider

00:28:22.649 --> 00:28:25.159
of the dragon Seasmoke.

00:28:25.159 --> 00:28:30.389
Marriage to Laenor will renew the Targaryen
alliance with the powerful Velaryons, to bring

00:28:30.389 --> 00:28:34.110
new strength and unity to the royal family.

00:28:34.110 --> 00:28:39.700
Rhaenyra reluctantly agrees to the marriage,
on the condition that Viserys remove Otto

00:28:39.700 --> 00:28:41.109
as Hand of the King.

00:28:41.109 --> 00:28:46.460
Rhaenyra knows that Otto is plotting against
her, trying to make Aegon heir instead of

00:28:46.460 --> 00:28:47.460
her.

00:28:47.460 --> 00:28:50.720
So Viserys agrees to remove his corrupt Hand.

00:28:50.720 --> 00:28:51.720
So in this scene, Viserys and Rhaenyra both
agree to make the smart political moves for

00:28:51.720 --> 00:28:52.720
the good of their house.

00:28:52.720 --> 00:28:53.720
Cause the stakes are high.

00:28:53.720 --> 00:28:54.720
If they don’t make the right alliances and
have secs with the right people, their dynasty

00:28:54.720 --> 00:28:55.720
will fall, the white walkers will win, and
the world will end.

00:28:55.720 --> 00:28:56.720
The drama in this story comes from the interconnection
of the personal, the political, and the magical.

00:28:56.720 --> 00:28:57.720
Viserys confronts Otto, and talks about his
father, Baelon Targaryen – the husband and

00:28:57.720 --> 00:28:59.789
brother of Alyssa.

00:28:59.789 --> 00:29:05.559
Prince “Baelon the Brave” was a warrior
– he rode the great dragon Vhagar, and wielded

00:29:05.559 --> 00:29:10.470
the Valyrian steel sword Dark Sister, now
used by Daemon.

00:29:10.470 --> 00:29:14.870
Baelon became Hand of the King to his father,
King Jaehaerys.

00:29:14.870 --> 00:29:20.210
And in the books, Baelon served as Hand for
over a year – he was effective, and popular

00:29:20.210 --> 00:29:22.399
with lords and common folk.

00:29:22.399 --> 00:29:27.899
But then Baelon died of a “burst belly”
– which might mean appendicitis.

00:29:27.899 --> 00:29:30.960
So Otto Hightower became the new Hand.

00:29:30.960 --> 00:29:37.809
Now, Viserys seems to suspect that Otto murdered
Baelon with poison or something, so that Otto

00:29:37.809 --> 00:29:39.350
could become Hand.

00:29:39.350 --> 00:29:44.970
Viserys is now deeply suspicious of Otto,
because Viserys has realised that Otto has

00:29:44.970 --> 00:29:47.479
been manipulating him for years.

00:29:47.479 --> 00:29:53.820
It was Otto’s plan for Alicent to hook up
Viserys, exploiting Viserys’ grief for his

00:29:53.820 --> 00:29:59.519
dead wife, to serve Otto’s ambition to get
his daughter married to the king.

00:29:59.519 --> 00:30:03.720
Viserys can no longer trust Otto, so he removes
him as Hand.

00:30:03.720 --> 00:30:09.259
Though the Hightowers remain a powerful and
ambitious family.

00:30:09.259 --> 00:30:12.989
Grand Maester Mellos brings Rhaenyra some
moon tea.

00:30:12.989 --> 00:30:16.609
This is the Westerosi version of a morning-after
pill.

00:30:16.609 --> 00:30:19.610
A plan B. Or plan tea.

00:30:19.610 --> 00:30:25.710
So if Rhaenyra got pregnant last night, this’ll
end the pregnancy, to prevent any troublesome

00:30:25.710 --> 00:30:28.240
royal bastards being born.

00:30:28.240 --> 00:30:31.809
Mellos says that Viserys sent Rhaenyra the
tea.

00:30:31.809 --> 00:30:38.389
But maybe Otto got Mellos to do it – Otto
doesn’t want Rhaenyra birthing any sons

00:30:38.389 --> 00:30:41.890
who might claim the Throne instead of Aegon.

00:30:41.890 --> 00:30:47.100
Mellos leaves, and the episode ends, so we
don’t know for sure if Rhaenyra drinks the

00:30:47.100 --> 00:30:48.100
tea.

00:30:48.100 --> 00:30:53.100
Maybe Criston Cole’s bastard son is growing
inside her.

00:30:53.100 --> 00:30:57.049
The last words in the episode are “unwanted
consequences”.

00:30:57.049 --> 00:31:03.009
Cause the characters make emotional decisions
that might come back to bite them – Daemon

00:31:03.009 --> 00:31:08.960
hooks up with Rhaenyra, Rhaenyra hooks up
with Criston and lies to Alicent, Viserys

00:31:08.960 --> 00:31:14.979
rejects Daemon and Otto, Mysaria spies for
Otto, and this Blackwood kills this Bracken

00:31:14.979 --> 00:31:19.989
– all these acts could lead to bigger conflicts
later on.

00:31:19.989 --> 00:31:25.450
King Viserys is getting sicker and weaker
each episode, and when he dies, there will

00:31:25.450 --> 00:31:28.669
be multiple conflicting claimants to his Throne.

00:31:28.669 --> 00:31:34.639
There’s a shot of rats on a dragon skull,
like scavengers feasting on the corpse of

00:31:34.639 --> 00:31:36.230
House Targaryen.

00:31:36.230 --> 00:31:40.460
Everyone’s choices now could have “unwanted
consequences”, shaping the conflicts to

00:31:40.460 --> 00:31:41.480
come.

00:31:41.480 --> 00:31:46.799
If you want to know more about Baelon the
Brave and Alyssa and Saera in the reign of

